# Input graph written at repair (2026-10-30) for
# CatholicOS__ontokit-api__ontokit_services_ontology_extractor.py__OntologyMetadataExtractor__extract_description.
# The only owl:Ontology has no description; the descriptions sit on
# neighbours that share two of the three terms of the global read
# `?s rdf:type owl:Ontology`:
#  - ex:NotAnOntology is typed, but owl:Class (object differs);
#  - ex:SeeAlsoOntology reaches owl:Ontology by rdfs:seeAlso (predicate
#    differs).
# With ontology_iri=None the region must return None: widening either term
# of the global read into a variable, or the subject of the reads in the
# global loop, returns one of the descriptions below instead.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
@prefix dc: <http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

ex:OntoBare a owl:Ontology .

ex:NotAnOntology a owl:Class ;
    dc:description "Typed, but not an ontology." .

ex:SeeAlsoOntology rdfs:seeAlso owl:Ontology ;
    dc:description "Linked to owl:Ontology by another predicate." .
